2026-09-27T03:28:09.4069147Z Description:
2026-09-27T03:28:09.4069945Z This PPA contains more recent Python versions packaged for Ubuntu.
2026-09-27T03:28:09.4070533Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:09.4071775Z Disclaimer: there's no guarantee of timely updates in case of security problems or other issues. If you want to use them in a security-or-otherwise-critical environment (say, on a production server), you do so at your own risk.
2026-09-27T03:28:09.4073162Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:09.4073293Z Update Note
2026-09-27T03:28:09.4073581Z ===========
2026-09-27T03:28:09.4074043Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T03:28:09.4074473Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:09.4074602Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T03:28:09.4074923Z ================
2026-09-27T03:28:09.4075138Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:09.4075365Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T03:28:09.4075905Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T03:28:09.4076234Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:09.4076404Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T03:28:09.4076811Z ====================================
2026-09-27T03:28:09.4077101Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:09.4077348Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T03:28:09.4077909Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T03:28:09.4078434Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T03:28:09.4079787Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T03:28:09.4080643Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:09.4080832Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T03:28:09.4081520Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T03:28:09.4082426Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T03:28:09.4082891Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:09.4083393Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T03:28:09.4084090Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:09.4084226Z Packages
2026-09-27T03:28:09.4084518Z ========
2026-09-27T03:28:09.4084703Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:09.4086969Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T03:28:09.4089474Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:09.4089844Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T03:28:09.4090631Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T03:28:09.4091408Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T03:28:09.4092419Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T03:28:09.4093365Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T03:28:09.4094092Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T03:28:09.4094553Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:09.4095167Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T03:28:09.4095585Z ==========================
2026-09-27T03:28:09.4095824Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:09.4097659Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T03:28:09.4183259Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:09.4184403Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T03:28:09.4186054Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T03:28:09.4186376Z 
